WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.295
Exploitation and initial execution are where a possible intrusion starts to produce

00:00:04.295 --> 00:00:06.043
observable behavior in the environment.

00:00:06.043 --> 00:00:10.937
At this point, a weakness may be triggered, unsafe input may reach vulnerable logic,

00:00:10.937 --> 00:00:14.433
or a user action may cause untrusted content to run.

00:00:14.433 --> 00:00:17.579
The defensive task is to connect evidence without overclaiming.

00:00:17.579 --> 00:00:18.628
Did something execute?

00:00:18.628 --> 00:00:21.775
Which account, process, host, workload, or application was involved?

00:00:21.775 --> 00:00:23.173
What changed immediately afterward?

00:00:23.173 --> 00:00:26.319
Patching, secure configuration, input validation, least privilege, endpoint protection,

00:00:26.319 --> 00:00:29.465
and application telemetry all reduce risk at this stage,

00:00:29.465 --> 00:00:31.913
but the response still depends on evidence.

00:00:31.913 --> 00:00:34.360
One alert rarely tells the whole story.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:38.205
Analysts should build a timeline that connects delivery signals, process behavior,

00:00:38.205 --> 00:00:40.652
authentication events, application logs, and control decisions.

00:00:40.652 --> 00:00:44.498
Initial execution is also a place where prevention and detection meet.

00:00:44.498 --> 00:00:47.994
A blocked attempt may reveal a control working as intended;

00:00:47.994 --> 00:00:51.490
a successful execution may require containment and deeper scope review.

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:53.587
Keep the analysis conceptual and authorized.

00:00:53.587 --> 00:00:57.782
The goal is to determine what happened, how confident the team is,

00:00:57.782 --> 00:01:01.278
and what response decision is justified by the available evidence.

00:01:01.278 --> 00:01:04.774
This stage is also a useful checkpoint for control validation.

00:01:04.774 --> 00:01:09.319
If a patch, hardening standard, or prevention control should have blocked the behavior,

00:01:09.319 --> 00:01:13.514
the team should verify whether the control was present, whether it worked,

00:01:13.514 --> 00:01:16.660
and whether any exception or coverage gap needs follow-up.
